Excerpts from netnews.rec.games.hack: 22-Mar-93 Re: Thirst in Nethack?
by Mike Marcelais@eos.ncsu. 
> How is the random number seeded?  You could just start two games with
> exactly the same number seed.  If they played the same way, the same things
> would happen.  Of course because the #s are grabed when needed. the
> dungeons would diverge but all would start equal.

NetHack tries to use the system time as the random number seed for
machines that have clocks (and the program knows about).  Excluding
changing the clock, the fact that your clock always gives a new and
unique seed means that *no* game will ever repeat....

If you want to change this, just change the setrandom function in
src/hacklib.c.

